    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The next time you see a globe, close your eyes and "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "spin",
            "zh": "使快速旋转"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " it quickly. Then stop it with your finger. You will probably land on a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "body of water",
            "zh": "水域"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". That’s because water covers 71 percent of the Earth’s surface. But if you don’t hit water, you might discover a place you’ve never heard of. Would you wonder who lives there and what it’s like?"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "These days, computers and smartphones can tell us exactly where we are and where we are going. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b1",
            "number": 1
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " Peter Bellerby, a globe maker in London, says this is because a globe “connects us to our planet”. With a globe, you can easily see what’s on the other side of the world from where you are. Joshua Nall is a museum director in England. He pointed out that technologies like Google Earth can provide students with more detailed information about the world. But the "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "physical",
            "ref": "v-physical"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " globe has become a symbol of knowledge. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b2",
            "number": 2
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Bellerby’s company makes about 600 globes a year. The process of making a globe begins with a "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "sphere",
            "zh": "球状物"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Workers place map pieces, called "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "“gores”",
            "zh": "地图切片"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ", onto the globe. The gores fit together to completely cover the sphere. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b3",
            "number": 3
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " They use deep blue and green for the oceans and yellow, green, and brown for the land. The designs can be complex."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p4",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "The world’s oldest "
          },
          {
            "t": "vocab",
            "v": "surviving",
            "ref": "v-surviving"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " globe dates from the 1490s. It is called the “Earth Apple”. Martin Behaim, a German explorer, made it. "
          },
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b4",
            "number": 4
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " You won’t find North or South America on it because Europeans hadn’t discovered them yet."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p5",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "blank",
            "id": "b5",
            "number": 5
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " They were made for British Prime Minister Winston Churchill and US President Franklin D. Roosevelt during WWII. They were each 1.2 metres in "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "diameter",
            "zh": "直径"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". A globe company in Chicago built them with help from 50 government geographers and mapmakers."
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "instruction": "Fill in each blank in the article with a proper sentence given below. Each sentence can be used only once. Note that there are two more sentences than you will need.",
      "bank": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Artists then paint the globe."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "But globes have remained popular."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Different kinds of people buy Bellerby’s products."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "People also buy globes as decorative pieces for their homes."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "E",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "There is the question of whether globes are useful or only works of art."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "F",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "The globe shows the world as people in the late 15th century understood it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "G",
          "content": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "Two of the world’s most famous globes were created about 450 years later."
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
